Package: azan-sip-client
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Azan SIP <noreply@github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Fudgeamin99/azan-sip-box
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), cage, xwayland, seatd, chromium, libgl1-mesa-dri, fonts-dejavu-core, alsa-utils, dbus, libpam-systemd, iproute2, libnss-mdns
Recommends: avahi-daemon, alsa-ucm-conf, firmware-intel-sound
Description: Azan SIP Box prayer times and azan on a TV, a Wyse or a laptop
 Turns a small Debian computer, such as a Dell Wyse thin client or an old
 laptop, 64-bit or 32-bit, into a TV screen for the Azan SIP Box. It shows
 the box's prayer-times screen full screen on the TV plugged into it (or the
 laptop's own screen), from every boot, and plays the azan through the TV's
 speakers (or the laptop's) at the same moment as the phones, at a volume
 of its own. It finds the box on the network, and reconnects by itself
 after the box restarts or the network drops.
